              "type": "text",
              "text": "Express the following in the form ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "R\\cos(x-\\alpha)",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q15",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{3}\\cos x+\\sin x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$",
          "worked": "Expand the requested form and equate coefficients.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{3}\\cos x+\\sin x&=R\\cos\\alpha\\cos x+R\\sin\\alpha\\sin x\\\\R\\cos\\alpha&=\\sqrt{3}\\\\R\\sin\\alpha&=1\\\\R&=\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^2+1^2}=2\\\\\\tan\\alpha&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth coefficients are positive, so choose $\\alpha$ in the first quadrant.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\\\\\sqrt{3}\\cos x+\\sin x&=2\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q16",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$3\\cos x+4\\sin x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5\\cos\\left(x-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\right)$",
          "worked": "Expand the requested form and equate coefficients.\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\cos x+4\\sin x&=R\\cos\\alpha\\cos x+R\\sin\\alpha\\sin x\\\\R\\cos\\alpha&=3\\\\R\\sin\\alpha&=4\\\\R&=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5\\\\\\tan\\alpha&=\\frac{4}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nBoth coefficients are positive, so choose $\\alpha$ in the first quadrant.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\\\3\\cos x+4\\sin x&=5\\cos\\left(x-\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q17",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x+\\sin x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$",
          "worked": "Expand the requested form and equate coefficients.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x+\\sin x&=R\\cos\\alpha\\cos x+R\\sin\\alpha\\sin x\\\\R\\cos\\alpha&=1\\\\R\\sin\\alpha&=1\\\\R&=\\sqrt{1^2+1^2}=\\sqrt{2}\\\\\\tan\\alpha&=1\\end{align*}$$\nBoth coefficients are positive, so choose $\\alpha$ in the first quadrant.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha&=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\\\\\cos x+\\sin x&=\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      }
    ]
  },
